+# Decision Record 001 — Architecture, scope, and cell semantics
+
+Date: 2026-09-22
+Status: **Accepted** (confirmed by user, round-2 Q&A)
+
+These are binding decisions. Later work must not silently contradict them; if a
+decision turns out to be wrong, supersede it with a new record rather than
+editing this one in place.
+
+---
+
+## D1 — Cell semantics and scheduling
+
+| Workspace | Role | Slots |
+|---|---|---|
+| Right rack (+X, 1.185 m, planes z=[0.55, 0.85], 3 jigs/plane) | **Incoming** | 6 |
+| Left rack (−X, 1.185 m, planes z=[0.25, 0.55, 0.85, 1.15], 4 jigs/plane) | **Outgoing** | 16 |
+| Table (+Y, 0.85 m, height 0.70) | **Inspection dwell** | 1 |
+
+- A **scheduler** owns slot assignment. It is a replaceable component, not
+  hard-coded into the task state machine.
+- Default scheduler traversal order: **top plane → bottom plane, then left → right**
+  within a plane. Applies to both picking from incoming and placing to outgoing.
+- **Refresh events:** incoming rack empty → request refill; outgoing rack full →
+  request removal. Both are external events; the cell pauses and signals.
+- **Inspection-complete trigger is UNDECIDED.** Implement as a
+  `InspectionSignal` protocol with a stub implementation (fixed dwell / manual
+  trigger). Do not bake a mechanism into the state machine.
+
+## D2 — AprilGrid label is physically fixed
+
+The 4×1 / 20 mm / 7.5 mm board stays as-is for now. Consequences:
+
+- Multi-view fusion and/or **reduced working distance** are the available levers.
+- **User-supplied mitigation:** the bottom plate + gripper can be inserted into
+  the *lower* shelf layer without colliding with that layer's tray. This lets
+  the flange advance well past the rack face, putting the EIH camera much closer
+  to the target layer's label. **Must be verified against the USD geometry**
+  (plane spacing 0.30 m vs. plate length 0.3265 m — the margin is thin).
+- Changing the label is reopenable **only with experimental evidence** from sim
+  showing 4×1 cannot meet the pitch budget.
+
+## D3 — USD assets are the authoritative geometry source
+
+All tray / jig / gripper / rack dimensions must be extracted programmatically
+from `tray_jig_with_label.usd`, `tray.usd`, `tm5s.usd` (and the `build_env`
+generators) during Phase 0. Numbers in `findings/01` that came from conversation
+are provisional and must be overwritten by extracted values.
+
+## D4 — Carry dynamics: conservative + tunable
+
+No mass or friction data available. Use a conservative cartesian
+acceleration/velocity cap on all carry segments, exposed as config
+(`grasp_profile.yaml: carry_limits`). Tighten or relax once measured.
+
+## D5 — Gripper behaviour
+
+- Jaws are **open** during approach and insertion.
+- After **lift**, jaws close to a position that **just fits the tray width**
+  (a width-fit close, not a force grip). Retention is plate + tilt + width fit.
+- On release, jaws reopen before the plate is withdrawn.
+- `change_load` (Techman) is a **placeholder** — define the call site in the
+  backend protocol, stub the implementation.
+
+## D6 — cuRobo
+
+- **cuRobo v2**, branch **`llm-wiki`** (this is effectively main).
+- v2 has its **own ESDF**; **nvblox / nvblox_torch is NOT required** and must not
+  be introduced as a dependency.
+- `dev/eef_cost` (bounded constraint planning) is a feature branch. If needed:
+  check out, finish/modify, **merge back into `llm-wiki`** rather than depending
+  on a long-lived fork.
+
+## D7 — MoveIt2 is vocabulary, not the planner
+
+Use MoveIt2 for **messages, TF, and RViz visualization only**:
+
+- `moveit_msgs/PlanningScene` + `AttachedCollisionObject` model the world and
+  the tray attach/detach lifecycle.
+- A dedicated **`curobo_planner` ROS2 node** owns all planning and exposes a
+  custom action supporting multi-waypoint goals, per-stage collision margin
+  profiles, and the mesh-collision metric toggle.
+- No cuRobo MoveIt planner plugin. No `move_group` in the control path.
+
+## D8 — Shared code: `shared/cell_core` vendored with drift detection
+
+- `shared/cell_core/` is the **single editable source** for pose math, config
+  schema, grasp sequencing, tolerance model. Pure Python; no ROS, no GPU.
+- `tools/sync_shared.py` copies it into `<repo>/vendor/cell_core` and writes a
+  hash manifest.
+- Each repo carries a unit test that **fails on hash drift**.
+- Rationale: air-gapped, no package registry, two independent repos.
+
+## D9 — ROS2 is the sim/real seam
+
+Isaac Sim and the real cell expose byte-identical ROS2 interfaces. The planner,
+perception, world-model, and task layers are unaware of which is running.
+Freezing this contract is a Phase 1 deliverable.
+
+## D10 — EIH focal configs are distance-dependent and must be selected
+
+Known anchor points supplied by the user:
+
+| Working distance | Focal config | fx / fy | cx / cy |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0.35 m | **6** | 2680.382 / 2680.745 | 1231.446 / 976.596 |
+| 0.12 m | **2** | 2653.350 / 2653.388 | 1232.009 / 979.569 |
+
+- Intrinsics **must** be chosen to match the commanded focal config. Using the
+  wrong set silently corrupts every pose estimate.
+- Config selection is therefore part of the **camera command interface**, not a
+  static calibration constant. The `CameraSource` protocol must expose it.
+- For distances other than 0.35 m and 0.12 m, the best config is **to be
+  determined experimentally** (sharpness/reprojection-error sweep in Phase 3).
+- Model this as `cameras.yaml: eih.focal_configs[]` with an
+  explicit `distance -> config` lookup table, seeded with the two known points
+  and extended as measurements accumulate.
+
+## D11 — Real-cell rack registration: deferred
+
+Sim-only for now. `env_shapes.yaml` poses are trusted as exact. Establishing
+rack poses against the true robot base is deferred until hardware bring-up.
+Design constraint: the world model must not *assume* config poses are exact, so
+a future aprilgrid-derived correction can be injected without redesign.
+
+## D12 — Git is user-managed
+
+`isaacsim/` and `program/` are already git repos, and remotes exist on the
+remote host. **The user performs all git operations.** The agent must not run
+`git init`, commit, branch, or push. The AgentOS git-safety checkpoint protocol
+stays **disabled** for this project.
+
+## D13 — CrossHost failures are escalated, never worked around
+
+Per `todo/plan.md` ("Problem on Crosshost"): on any unexpected behaviour of the
+`.crosshost` wrappers, **pause and ask the user**. Do not patch the scripts, and
+do not invent a bypass (e.g. writing files via heredoc because `sync.ps1` is
+failing). Report and wait.
+
+> Historical note: before this rule existed, `sync.ps1`/`fetch.ps1` were hanging
+> and the agent worked around them via `execute.ps1` heredocs. The user has since
+> fixed both scripts; file-mode sync and fetch are now verified working.
+
+## D14 — Carry limits derived, pending friction measurement
+
+Tray mass is **1.2 kg**. With the 15° tilt, forward retention is
+`a_max = g(μ cos θ + sin θ)`, which yields ≥ 2.99 m/s² even at μ = 0.05 — the
+tilt alone contributes 2.54 m/s². Lateral retention is friction-only and is
+therefore **carried by the jaw width-fit close (D5)**, not by the plate.
+
+Initial conservative caps (tunable, per D4): linear 1.5 m/s² / 0.25 m/s,
+angular 3.0 rad/s² / 0.5 rad/s, downward accel ≤ 4.0 m/s².
+See `findings/03 §6`.
+
+## D15 — ~~The close-sighting pose depends on the slot below~~ **SUPERSEDED by D18**
+
+> **Retracted 2026-09-22.** This decision rested on the wrong EIH camera offset.
+> The interference is 41.6 mm, not 3 mm, and no camera raise that fits in the
+> image can fix it. The close read moves out to 0.2118 m instead, at which point
+> the plate never enters the shelf and the pose is **independent** of the slot
+> below. The scheduler/world-model/look-pose coupling introduced here does not
+> exist. See D18 and `findings/03 §4`.
+
+~~At the real 0.25 m layer gap the reduced-standoff sighting pose (D2) collides
+with the tray on the layer below unless the EIH camera is raised ~23–33 mm above
+the label centre. The raise is not needed when the slot below is empty or when
+sighting the lowest layer. Therefore the look-pose generator is a function of
+world-model occupancy, not of the target slot alone.~~
+
+## D16 — Real cell parameters (confirmed)
+
+| | Incoming (right, +X) | Outgoing (left, −X) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Width × depth | 0.800 × 0.308 | 1.160 × 0.308 |
