+# Findings 01 — Cell geometry, grasp kinematics, and the tolerance budget
+
+> **SUPERSEDED (2026-09-22) by `findings/02-verified-usd-geometry.md`.**
+> Sections 4, 5 and 10 contain provisional numbers taken from conversation that
+> the USD extraction has since corrected (plate tip 0.3185 not 0.3265, plate
+> offset −0.0377 not −0.041, insertion travel ~0.282 not 0.245). The clearances
+> in §6 and the pitch risk in §7 were **confirmed** and still stand.
+> Read `findings/02` first; keep this file only for the reasoning history.
+
+Status: derived from user-supplied initial guesses + `todo/resources/isaacsim/camera_param_raw/`.
+**Not yet validated against the USD assets.** Everything here must be re-derived from
+`tray_jig_with_label.usd` / `tray.usd` / `tm5s.usd` in Phase 0 and this file updated.
+
+## 1. Frames
+
+Canonical convention for the whole project (decided in Phase 0, recorded here):
+
+- Length in metres, angles in radians.
+- Pose = `[x, y, z, qx, qy, qz, qw]` when serialised in YAML/config (matches the
+  hand-eye files the user supplied). Converted to cuRobo's `wxyz` at the cuRobo
+  boundary only, inside one adapter function.
+- `flange` = `link_6` tip = the frame the hand-eye extrinsics are expressed in.
+- Flange `+Z` is the approach axis (gripper/plate points along `+Z`).
+
+## 2. Hand-eye extrinsics (flange -> camera), as given
+
+| Camera | translation (m) | quaternion (x,y,z,w) | note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| EIH (5M) | `[-0.000197, 0.075155, 0.044217]` | `[-0.0028788, -0.0016772, -0.99999427, 0.00059817]` | ~180 deg about Z |
+| RealSense D455 | `[-0.0136189, 0.1176036, 0.0949444]` | `[0.0024163, -0.0113972, 0.99992952, -0.0022852]` | ~180 deg about Z |
+
+Both cameras sit close to the flange (z = 0.044 / 0.095) and look along the
+approach axis. **The bottom plate extends to z = 0.3265, i.e. ~0.28 m beyond the
+EIH camera.** The plate is therefore always in the near field / possibly in
+frame during approach.
+
+## 3. Intrinsics
+
+- EIH: 2592x1944, `plumb_bob`. Eight selectable focal configs.
+  - Config 1: fx=2773.317, fy=2773.813, cx=1228.326, cy=974.060,
+    d=[0.1798, -0.4659, 0.0004, 0.0005, 0.1451]
+  - Config 2: fx=2653.350, fy=2653.388, cx=1232.009, cy=979.569,
+    d=[0.1088, 0.2705, 0.0007, 0.0003, -1.8604]
+  - Configs 3..8 in `camera_param_raw/eih_camera_intrinsics.md`.
+  - **Open item:** which config maps to which physical focal setting, and how the
+    focal setting is commanded at runtime.
+- D455: 640x480, fx=387.529, fy=387.039, cx=320.054, cy=248.644,
+  d=[-0.0548339, 0.0632865, -0.00088626, 0.00065029, -0.02045422]
+
+## 4. Gripper / bottom plate
+
+- `flange -> plate tip` = `[0, -0.041, 0.3265]`
+- Bottom plate size = `[0.06, 0.01, 0.3265]` (width X, thickness Y, length Z)
+- Plate is offset `-0.041` in flange Y (hangs to one side of the approach axis).
+
+## 5. Grasp sequence arithmetic (derived)
+
+Let `d` = distance from flange origin to the aprilgrid plane, measured along the
+approach axis.
+
+| Stage | `d` (m) | plate tip vs. grid plane (m) | note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Pre-insert (look/grasp start) | 0.3465 | -0.020 (tip 20 mm short of plane) | |
+| +0.045 forward: "ready to insert" | 0.3015 | +0.025 past plane | tip has entered the jig mouth |
+| +0.200 forward: fully inserted | 0.1015 | +0.225 into the jig | 225 mm of plate under the tray |
+
+Total forward travel from pre-insert to full insertion: **0.245 m**.
+At full insertion the EIH camera is only ~0.0575 m from the label plane, so the
+camera is useless past the "ready to insert" point — all visual servoing, if any,
+must finish before then.
+
+Then: lift `0.04`, retreat (reverse of the 0.245 m), tilt `15 deg`.
+
+## 6. Clearances -> accuracy requirement (THE driving constraint)
+
+Tray-on-column pocket: height `0.030`, width `0.105`. Plate: thickness `0.010`,
+width `0.060`.
+
+- Vertical slack: `0.030 - 0.010 = 0.020` m total => **+/- 0.010 m** if centred.
+- Lateral slack: `0.105 - 0.060 = 0.045` m total => **+/- 0.0225 m** if centred.
+
+Over the `0.225` m insertion depth this converts to an angular budget:
+
+- Yaw (rotation about the vertical axis): `asin(0.0225 / 0.225)` ~= **5.7 deg**
+- Pitch (rotation about the horizontal axis, i.e. plate tipping): `asin(0.010 / 0.225)` ~= **2.5 deg**
+
+These are *total* budgets and must be shared between aprilgrid pose error,
+hand-eye calibration error, robot absolute accuracy, and tray-seating error on
+the columns. A reasonable split leaves roughly **1 deg of pitch** for the vision
+estimate alone.
+
+## 7. RISK: the aprilgrid is badly conditioned for pitch
+
+Board layout from `create_rack_shelf_with_tray_jig.py`:
+`tags_x=4, tags_y=1, tag_size=0.020, tag_separation=0.0075`
+=> board extent = `4*0.020 + 3*0.0075 = 0.1025` m wide by **`0.020` m tall**.
+
+A 4x1 planar target is nearly a *line*. Planar-pose estimation error about the
+long axis scales inversely with the target's extent perpendicular to that axis
+(here only 20 mm). This is exactly the pitch DOF with the **tightest (2.5 deg)**
+budget. Single-shot pitch from this board is likely to be the dominant error term.
+
+Mitigations to evaluate, in order of preference:
+1. **Multi-view fusion** — observe the same board from 2-3 arm poses with
+   deliberate baseline. Parallax conditions the out-of-plane rotation far better
+   than any single shot. Costs cycle time; needs a pose-graph / weighted fusion.
+2. **Get closer + pick the sharpest focal config** — at d=0.3465 with fx~2773,
+   the 20 mm dimension spans ~160 px. Halving the distance doubles that.
+3. **Change the label to 4x2 or add a second board** on a different jig face.
+   Requires a physical change; only worth raising if 1 and 2 are insufficient.
+
+Do not assume single-shot detection is adequate. Quantify it in sim first
+(ground-truth pose is available there) before building the pick pipeline on it.
+
+## 8. Environment layout (from `env_setup.md` defaults)
+
+Robot at origin facing +Y. Right rack at +X (1.185 m, planes z=[0.55, 0.85], 3
+jigs/plane), left rack at -X (1.185 m, planes z=[0.25, 0.55, 0.85, 1.15], 4
+jigs/plane), table at +Y (0.85 m, height 0.70). Robot leg height 0.5.
+AprilGrid ids assigned sequentially: right rack (bottom plane, left-to-right),
+then left rack, then table.
+
+Total addressable slots: right 2*3 = 6, left 4*4 = 16, table 1. **23 slots.**
+
+Roles (see `decisions/001`): **right = incoming**, **left = outgoing**,
+**table = inspection dwell**.
+
+## 9. Open items
+
+Resolved in `decisions/001-architecture-and-scope.md`:
+rack roles (D1), label fixed (D2), USD authoritative (D3), conservative tunable
+accel cap (D4), gripper width-fit close after lift (D5), cuRobo v2 `llm-wiki`
+with built-in ESDF and no nvblox (D6).
+
+Still open, to be closed by **extraction from the USD assets in Phase 0**:
+
+- Column height above the shelf plane (confirm the 0.04 m lift clears it).
+- Gripper jaw open width and the tray width it closes onto.
+- Exact pocket clearance (currently assumed 0.030 x 0.105).
+- Shelf plane spacing vs. plate length: planes are 0.30 m apart but the plate is
+  0.3265 m long. This gates the D2 "insert into the lower layer to get closer"
+  mitigation -- see section 10.
+
+Still open, requiring user/external input:
+
+- Inspection-complete trigger mechanism (placeholder for now).
+- Tray mass / friction (conservative default for now).
+- Which EIH focal config corresponds to which physical focal setting, and how
+  the setting is commanded at runtime.
+- Real-cell registration: how rack poses in `env_shapes.yaml` are established
+  against the true robot base (survey vs. derived from observed aprilgrids).
+
+## 10. Reduced-standoff mitigation (from D2) -- to verify
+
+User states the bottom plate + gripper can enter the **lower** shelf layer
+without hitting that layer's tray, letting the flange advance past the rack face
+so the EIH camera gets close to the *target* layer's label.
+
+Arithmetic to check against the USDs:
+
+- Shelf plane spacing = `0.30` m; plate length from flange = `0.3265` m.
+- Plate hangs at flange `Y = -0.041`, i.e. **below** the flange axis if the
+  gripper points horizontally with the plate down. So when the camera is
+  sighting the label on plane `N`, the plate sweeps a corridor ~`0.041` m below
+  the flange -- which must clear plane `N-1`'s tray and columns.
+- If clearance holds, standoff drops from `0.3465` m to roughly `0.10-0.15` m,
+  which would grow the 20 mm board dimension from ~160 px to ~370-550 px and
+  materially improve the pitch estimate.
+
+**Risk:** this puts the plate deep inside the rack during a *pre-grasp sighting*
+move, so a bad pose estimate now risks a collision rather than just a failed
+insert. The collision margin profile for the "close sighting" stage must be
+derived from the USD geometry, not guessed. Verify before adopting.
