+# Findings 02 — VERIFIED cell geometry (extracted from USD assets)
+
+> **PARTIALLY SUPERSEDED (2026-09-22) by `findings/03-real-rack-and-tray-underside.md`
+> and `findings/04-reachability-sweep.md`.**
+> Robot, gripper, plate, jaw, jig and tray dimensions below remain authoritative.
+> But four things changed:
+> - **§8/§9's EIH camera offset is WRONG.** This document put the camera at flange
+>   `+Y 0.0752 / +Z 0.0442`. It is actually **`+Y 0.11383 / +Z 0.10670`**, confirmed
+>   twice independently: by re-measuring all five camera prims in `tm5s.usd`
+>   (`tools/verify_flange_offsets.py`), and by the commented-out
+>   `joint_link_6-Camera` in `tm5s_v4.urdf` (`xyz="-0.0002088 0.113722 0.106752"`).
+>   Camera→plate-bottom is **0.15652**, not 0.1129. **§9's "VERIFIED VIABLE"
+>   conclusion is retracted** — see below and `findings/03` §4.
+> - §7 assumed `plane_thickness = 0.030`; it is **0.020**, so the label centre is
+>   at `h − 0.005`, not `h`.
+> - §9's D2 clearance used the **sim** 0.30 m layer gap. The real racks use
+>   **0.25 m**. With the corrected camera offset the true clearance is
+>   **−41.6 mm** (interference), not +47 mm and not the −3 mm quoted in the first
+>   revision of this header.
+> - §6's vertical slack ignored the tray's underside recess, measured at
+>   **2.50 mm** (not 3 mm), which loosens the pitch budget from 2.55° to 2.87°.
+> Read `findings/03` and `findings/04` for the corrected numbers. All derived
+> geometry now lives in `tools/cell_geometry.py`; do not transcribe numbers out of it.
+
+Status: **authoritative** for the asset dimensions themselves. Extracted 2026-09-22 from the USD assets on the
+isaacsim host via `pxr` (read-only). Supersedes the provisional numbers in
+`findings/01`, which came from conversation.
+
+Method: `_p0/dump_usd_geometry.py` + `report{,2,3}.py` on `10.105.21.1`.
+Meshes were transformed into the **flange frame** to get true profiles rather
+than inflated world AABBs.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Frame conventions (confirmed from `tm5s.usd`)
+
+At the zero joint configuration the flange basis in world coordinates is:
+
+| Flange axis | World direction | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `+X` | `+X` | gripper open/close axis |
+| `+Y` | `+Z` (up) | "up"; the bottom plate hangs at **−Y** |
+| `+Z` | `−Y` | **approach axis** (insertion direction) |
+
+`/tm5s/flange` is coincident with `/tm5s/link_6` (zero offset, identity
+rotation), world `T = [0, -0.28275, 1.0949]` at zero config. The hand-eye
+extrinsics are expressed in this frame.
+
+All stages: `metersPerUnit = 1.0`, `upAxis = Z`. Units are metres.
+
+## 2. TM5S kinematics (from physics joints)
+
+| Joint | Parent offset | Axis | Limits (deg) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| joint_1 | `[0, 0, 0.1484]` | Z | ±360 |
+| joint_2 | `[0, 0, 0]`, rot `[-0.5, -0.5, -0.5, 0.5]` | Z | ±360 |
+| joint_3 | `[0.429, 0, 0]` | Z | ±158 |
+| joint_4 | `[0.386, 0, -0.1478]`, rot `[0,0,0.7071,0.7071]` | Z | ±360 |
+| joint_5 | `[0, -0.1315, 0]`, rot `[0.7071,0,0,0.7071]` | Z | ±360 |
+| joint_6 | `[0, -0.13495, 0]`, rot `[0.7071,0,0,0.7071]` | Z | ±360 |
+
+Link masses: 1.0 / 4.32 / 9.796 / 2.778 / 1.77 / 1.77 / 2.313 kg.
+Gripper body 1.49 kg, each jaw 0.10 kg, D455 0.103 kg.
+
+## 3. Gripper — bottom plate profile (flange frame)
+
+Sliced `/tm5s/link_6/gripper_body/visuals/mesh_23` (9389 pts) along flange `+Z`:
+
+| Region | flange `z` | X width | Y (vertical) extent |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Gripper body | `0.000 – 0.100` | 0.122 – 0.130 | `[-0.0427, +0.0393]` (0.082) |
+| **Bottom plate** | **`0.100 – 0.3185`** | **0.060** | **`[-0.0427, -0.0327]` (0.010)** |
+
+So the corrected plate parameters:
+
+| Quantity | **Verified** | Previously assumed |
+|---|---|---|
+| Plate width (X) | **0.060** | 0.06 ✓ |
+| Plate thickness (Y) | **0.010** | 0.01 ✓ |
+| Plate tip, flange `z` | **0.3185** | 0.3265 ✗ |
+| Plate vertical centre, flange `Y` | **−0.0377** | −0.041 ✗ |
+| Plate top / bottom surface, flange `Y` | **−0.0327 / −0.0427** | — |
+
+## 4. Gripper jaws — stroke and the straddle requirement
+
+Finger tips occupy flange `z ∈ [0.2426, 0.2804]`, vertical extent
+`Y ∈ [-0.0336, +0.0384]` (72 mm tall), and are thin (1.5 mm) in X.
+
+| Joint value | Left finger X | Right finger X | **Inner gap** |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `0` (home) | −0.0497 | +0.0494 | **0.098** |
+| `±0.05` (full open) | −0.0997 | +0.0994 | **0.198** |
+
+Prismatic limits: left `[-0.05, 0]`, right `[0, +0.05]`, axis X.
+
+**Consequence — the jaws MUST be open during insertion.** The tray is
+**0.1329 m** wide, which is wider than the 0.098 m home gap. The fingers
+therefore cannot pass the tray while closed; they must be opened to
+`gap > 0.133` so they straddle the tray on the way in.
+
+The D5 "close to just fit the tray width" target is `gap = 0.1329`, i.e. each
+jaw at `±0.01745` — comfortably inside the `±0.05` stroke. **D5 is achievable.**
+
+## 5. Tray (`tray.usd`)
+
+The prim carries a uniform scale `0.02543` **and** a −90° Z rotation, so the
+world AABB is misleading. True dimensions from local mesh points × scale:
+
+**Tray = `0.1329 (X) × 0.2470 (Y) × 0.0851 (Z)`** in the jig-aligned orientation.
+
+## 6. Tray jig (`tray_jig_with_label.usd`) — all exact
+
+Base plate: `0.156 × 0.270 × 0.005`, occupying jig `z ∈ [0, 0.005]`.
+
+Four columns, each `0.025 (X) × 0.020 (Y) × 0.030 (Z)`, centred at
+`(±0.0655, ±0.1250, 0.020)` → each spans jig `z ∈ [0.005, 0.035]`.
+
+**The insertion pocket** (where the bottom plate goes):
+
+| Axis | Extent | Clearance |
+|---|---|---|
+| `z` (height) | `0.005 → 0.035` | **0.030** vs. 0.010 plate → **±0.010** |
+| `x` (width) | `−0.053 → +0.053` | **0.106** vs. 0.060 plate → **±0.023** |
+| `y` (depth) | `−0.115 → +0.115` clear between columns | 0.230 |
+
+**Both clearance assumptions in `findings/01` are confirmed** (0.030 height,
+0.106 ≈ the assumed 0.105 width). The tolerance budget stands:
+
+- Yaw budget `asin(0.023 / 0.225) ≈ 5.9°`
+- **Pitch budget `asin(0.010 / 0.225) ≈ 2.5°`** ← still the binding constraint
+
+Tray seating: tray half-width 0.0665 rests on columns spanning `x ∈ [0.053, 0.078]`;
+tray half-length 0.1235 rests on columns spanning `y ∈ [0.115, 0.135]`. Tray
+occupies jig `z ∈ [0.035, 0.1201]`.
+
+## 7. Label / AprilGrid placement
+
+`label_base` front face (`Cube_07`) is `0.1125 × 0.0005 × 0.0300` at
+`(0, 0.1570, −0.0150)`, i.e.:
+
+- Label plane at **jig `y = +0.157`**
+- Label spans **jig `z ∈ [−0.030, 0.000]`** — *below* the jig base plate
+
+From `create_rack_shelf_with_tray_jig.py`: the grid is `4 × 1`, `markerLength
+0.020`, `separation 0.0075`, `margin 0.005`, family `DICT_APRILTAG_36h11`, ids
+assigned `grid_id * 4 + [0..3]`.
+
+→ **grid = `0.1025 × 0.020`** centred on the `0.1125 × 0.030` plate. Confirms the
+pitch-conditioning risk in `findings/01 §7`.
+
+Rack placement: `JIG_Y_OFFSET = 0.135`, so jig centre is at rack `y = size_y − 0.135`
+and the label sits at rack `y = size_y + 0.022` (protruding 22 mm past the rack face).
+Shelf planes are solid cubes of thickness `0.03` centred at height `h`, so the
+label spans exactly `z ∈ [h − 0.015, h + 0.015]` — **the label is mounted on the
+shelf's front edge face.**
+
+## 8. Insertion geometry (derived)
+
+Let the flange origin sit at rack `y = Y0`; a feature at flange `z` maps to
+rack `y = Y0 − z`.
+
+For full insertion (plate tip reaching the far column inner face, jig `y = −0.115`):
+`Y0 = −0.115 + 0.3185 = 0.2035` (jig frame).
+
+- Flange stays **0.0465 m in front of the label plane** — it never passes it.
+- ~~EIH camera (flange `+Z` offset `0.0442`) ends at jig `y = 0.1593`~~ **WRONG —
+  the camera `+Z` offset is `0.10670`.** Corrected: the camera ends at jig
+  `y = 0.2035 − 0.10670 = 0.0968`, i.e. **60 mm short of** the label plane, so it
+  goes blind well before full insertion rather than exactly at it.
+- Fingers end at jig `y ∈ [−0.077, −0.039]` — **between** the column pairs at
+  `y = ±0.125`, so open jaws do not strike the columns. ✓
+- Starting with the tip 10 mm clear of the label plane, **total insertion travel
+  ≈ 0.282 m**, and the natural pre-insert EIH standoff is **≈ 0.284 m**.
+
+## 9. D2 reduced-standoff mitigation — ~~**VERIFIED VIABLE**~~ **RETRACTED**
+
+> **This whole section is wrong and its conclusion is retracted.** It rests on a
+> camera offset that is off by ~44 mm, and on the sim's 0.30 m layer gap rather
+> than the real 0.25 m. The corrected analysis is in `findings/03` §4: at the real
+> layer gap the plate **interferes with the tray below by 41.6 mm**, and the fix is
+> to *increase* the standoff to ≥ 0.2118 m, not decrease it to 0.12 m.
+> `findings/04` §4 shows that doing so costs no reachability.
+> Kept below only as a record of the error.
+
+Question: at a 0.12 m EIH standoff (focal config 2), does the gripper clear the
+shelf below?
+
+Camera sits at the label centre height `z = h`. ~~From the hand-eye and plate
+geometry the plate is `0.0752 + 0.0377 = 0.1129` below the camera.~~
+**WRONG — the true camera→plate-bottom distance is `0.15652`** (camera at flange
+`+Y 0.11383`, plate bottom at flange `+Y −0.04269`).
+
+| Item | World z |
+|---|---|
+| Shelf N plate | `h − 0.015 → h + 0.015` |
+| **Bottom plate** | **`h − 0.118 → h − 0.108`** |
+| Finger bottom | `h − 0.1088` |
+| Shelf N−1 plate top | `h − 0.285` |
+| **Tray on shelf N−1, top** | **`h − 0.165`** |
+
+- Plate passes **under shelf N** (93 mm below it). ✓
+- Plate passes **over the tray on shelf N−1** with **≈ 47 mm clearance**. ✓
+- Fingers clear the lower tray by **≈ 56 mm**. ✓
+
+Horizontally the plate tip reaches rack `y = size_y − 0.1325`, i.e. 132 mm inside
+the rack face, directly above the lower tray.
+
+**Conclusion: the reduced-standoff sighting pose is geometrically feasible with
+~47 mm of vertical margin.** This is the preferred fix for the pitch-accuracy
+risk — it is cheaper than multi-view fusion and needs no physical change.
+
+**Caveats to carry into Phase 3:**
+1. 47 mm must absorb robot absolute accuracy, rack registration error, and the
+   lower tray's own seating error. Budget it explicitly.
+2. This pose puts the plate deep inside the rack *before* a good pose estimate
+   exists. The collision margin profile for "close sighting" must come from this
+   geometry, not a guess.
+3. The topmost shelf has no shelf above it and the bottom shelf no tray below —
+   clearance varies per plane. Verify per-slot, not once.
+
