+# Reachability volume report
+
+**Date:** 2026-10-07 (made in `.custom-workspace/`; ingested here 2026-10-10, D29.
+Code in [tools/reach_volume/](../tools/reach_volume/), data and plots in
+[renders/reach_volume/](../renders/reach_volume/). The D29 gripper fix changed
+only the collision cubes, not the spheres used in section 6, so the results stand.)
+**Preset:** `strict` (standoff_far 0.35 m, standoff_near 0.2768 m, `carry_tilt_deg` unset = 0)
+**Solver:** EAIK analytic IK, TM5S joint limits from `tm5s_v4.urdf`
+
+## 1. Question
+
+Where in space, relative to the robot base, can the arm perform the grasp
+sequence, and how far through the sequence does it get?
+
+## 2. Method
+
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Frame | Robot base, origin (0, 0, 0), +Z up |
+| Search space | x in [-1.2, 1.2], y in [0, 1.4], z in [-1.2, 1.2] m |
+| Grid | 50 mm, 49 x 29 x 49 = 69,629 points |
+| Gripper | Parallel to the ground, pointing +Y. Same rotation at every point |
+| Grid point means | The centre of a tray's AprilGrid (the label), not the flange |
+| Poses per point | The 7 phases of `cell_core.sequence.grasp_sequence`, derived from that point |
+| Step reached | Walk the phases in order; stop at the first IK failure. Level = phases solved |
+
+Phase order: 1 `sight_far`, 2 `sight_near`, 3 `pre_insert`, 4 `insert`,
+5 `lift`, 6 `withdraw`, 7 `carry`.
+
+**Reuse.** Pose construction is `cell_core.sequence`; the IK solve, URDF joint
+limits and flange-frame correction are `reach_sweep.py`. Each grid point is
+turned into a "probe slot" so the existing pose code runs unchanged.
+
+**Validation** ([test_reach_volume.py](../tools/reach_volume/test_reach_volume.py), 3 passed):
+- The probe slot regenerates the flange poses of all 37 real `strict` slots to 1e-9 m.
+- All 37 real slots reach level 7 through this code path, matching the recorded 259/259.
+- A point at (1.2, 1.4, 1.2) reaches nothing.
+
+## 3. Result
+
+| Level | Last step reached | Points | x range (m) | y range (m) | z range (m) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | none | 48,973 | | | |
+| 1 | `sight_far` | 1,851 | -0.80 .. 0.80 | 0.05 .. 1.35 | -0.70 .. 1.15 |
+| 2 | `sight_near` | 1,855 | -0.80 .. 0.80 | 0.00 .. 1.25 | -0.65 .. 1.15 |
+| 3 | `pre_insert` | 4,518 | -0.80 .. 0.80 | 0.00 .. 1.25 | -0.70 .. 1.00 |
+| 4 | `insert` | 146 | -0.80 .. 0.80 | 0.00 .. 1.00 | -0.45 .. 1.00 |
+| 5 | `lift` | 80 | -0.75 .. 0.75 | 0.00 .. 0.35 | 0.05 .. 0.95 |
+| 6 | `withdraw` | 0 | | | |
+| 7 | `carry` (full sequence) | 12,206 | -0.80 .. 0.80 | 0.00 .. 1.00 | -0.70 .. 0.95 |
+
+20,656 of 69,629 points (29.7 %) reach at least one step; 12,206 (17.5 %)
+complete the whole sequence.
+
+### Observations
+
+1. **The full-sequence region is a shell around the base, out to y = 1.0 m.**
+   Its cross-section shrinks with distance: at y = 0.5 it spans x +/-0.75 and
+   z -0.70..0.90; at y = 0.8, x +/-0.55 and z -0.60..0.75; at y = 1.0, only
+   x +/-0.25 and z -0.30..0.40 (141 points).
+2. **Sighting reaches furthest, motion reaches least.** `sight_far` and
+   `sight_near` go out to y = 1.25-1.35 m, because the camera stops
+   `standoff` short of the label. Level 1-2 points with y >= 1.0 m number 1,307.
+   Those are points where the camera can look but the gripper cannot reach.
+3. **`insert` and `lift` are the binding steps.** Of 4,518 points that clear
+   `pre_insert`, only 146 clear `insert` on their own and 80 stop at `lift`.
+   The `lift` stoppers are all within y <= 0.35 m of the base: the plate must
+   be both deep and raised there, which runs into the joint limits.
+4. **Level 6 is empty because `carry_tilt_deg` is 0 in `strict`.** The `carry`
+   pose is `withdraw` with the plate tilted by that angle; at 0 it is the same
+   pose, so `carry` succeeds exactly when `withdraw` does. Level 7 is therefore
+   "up to `withdraw`", not evidence for the tilt. Setting a tilt (0-30 deg is
+   permitted) would separate the two levels. This also corrects my earlier
+   chat remark that `withdraw` "never shows as level 6 because carry also
+   fails"; the cause is the zero tilt.
+### Largest slices (full-sequence points)
+
+First slice with the maximum count (ties not checked).
+
+| Axis | Position | Points |
+|---|---|---|
+| x | -0.20 m | 605 |
+| y | 0.35 m | 720 |
+| z | 0.00 m | 503 |
+
+## 4. Limits of this result (IK-only run, sections 1-3)
+
+- **Kinematics only.** No collision check against the robot's own body, the
+  racks, shelves or table. Section 6 adds self-collision; the world is still
+  not checked. For cell geometry, use the cuRobo collision report (M3).
+- **Grid is a probe, not a rack.** Every point is treated as a free-standing
+  label with a +Y approach. Real racks fix both the approach and the layer
+  heights; the slot sweep remains the authority for the cell.
+- **Resolution.** 50 mm grid; thin features (the 80-point `lift` set, the 146
+  `insert` points) are only a few cells thick and their edges are +/-50 mm.
+- **Chain stops at first failure.** A point whose `sight_far` fails shows no dot
+  even if `insert` alone would solve. This is the requested definition.
+- **Gripper rotation is fixed.** Only the +Y orientation is swept; other yaws
+  would give a different volume.
+- **IK criterion.** "Reached" means an exact analytic solution inside the URDF
+  joint limits (position tolerance 1e-4 m, rotation 1e-3 rad). No branch
+  continuity between phases is enforced, unlike the M3 chain check.
+
+## 5. Files
+
+| File | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| [reach_volume.py](../tools/reach_volume/reach_volume.py) | Runs the sweep, writes `reach_volume.npz` |
+| [reach_volume.npz](../renders/reach_volume/reach_volume.npz) | Raw result: axes, `levels` (int8), phase names |
+| [plot_reach_volume.py](../tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_volume.py) -> `reach_volume.html` | 3D scatter, colour = last step, no dot for level 0 |
+| [plot_reach_slices.py](../tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_slices.py) -> `reach_slices.html` | Slice viewer with sliders along x, y and z |
+| [test_reach_volume.py](../tools/reach_volume/test_reach_volume.py) | Cross-check against the real slot sweep |
+| [reach_volume_curobo.py](../tools/reach_volume/reach_volume_curobo.py) | Section 6 run, on the program host; writes `reach_volume_curobo.npz` |
+| [reach_volume_curobo.npz](../renders/reach_volume/reach_volume_curobo.npz) | `levels` (self-collision-free) and `levels_ik` (IK only) |
+| `reach_volume_curobo.html`, `reach_slices_curobo.html` | The same two plots for the self-collision result; the 3D plot has a hidden legend entry for the points lost to self-collision |
+
+**Reproduce**
+
+```powershell
+python .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/reach_volume.py            # ~40 s at 50 mm
+python .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_volume.py
+python .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_slices.py
+python -m pytest .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/test_reach_volume.py -q --import-mode=importlib -p no:cacheprovider
+```
+
+Options: `--step 0.025` for a finer grid, `--preset recommended` for another
+cell, `--x/--y/--z LO HI` to change the search box.
+
+## 6. With cuRobo self-collision
+
+**Change.** A phase now counts as reached only if some exact, in-limit EAIK
+branch is also free of self-collision. Everything else is as before: same grid,
+same +Y gripper, same stop-at-first-failure walk.
+
+**Self-collision test.** cuRobo's own self-collision distance for the TM5S arm
+plus the egu50 gripper (jaws open, 0.04 m), using the robot config on the
+program host. A configuration collides when that distance is above 0, the same
+criterion as `check_cell.py` (`pose_ok`). It is a sphere model, so it is
+conservative. No world obstacles are used.
+
+**Checks run before trusting it**
+- All 37 real `strict` slots, every phase, still have a self-free branch
+  (agrees with the M3 collision PASS 37/37).
+- The IK-only level computed in the same run equals `reach_volume.npz` at all
+  69,629 points (exact array equality), so the only difference is the new test.
+- The test is not vacuous: 42,368 of 108,463 `sight_far` branches self-collide.
+
+**Result**
+
+| Level | Last step reached | IK only | + self-collision |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | none | 48,973 | 50,711 |
+| 1 | `sight_far` | 1,851 | 1,745 |
+| 2 | `sight_near` | 1,855 | 2,064 |
+| 3 | `pre_insert` | 4,518 | 4,114 |
+| 4 | `insert` | 146 | 149 |
+| 5 | `lift` | 80 | 106 |
+| 6 | `withdraw` | 0 | 0 |
+| 7 | `carry` (full sequence) | 12,206 | 10,740 |
+
+Levels 2, 4 and 5 grow because points that used to go further now stop there.
+No point reaches further than before.
+
+- **Any step:** 20,656 points -> 18,918. **Full sequence:** 12,206 -> 10,740, a
+  loss of 1,466 points (12 %).
+- **Where the loss is.** Close to the base. By horizontal distance from the base
+  axis, of the IK-complete points: r < 0.3 m, 680 of 1,168 lost; 0.3-0.6 m,
+  652 of 3,964; 0.6-0.9 m, 134 of 5,750; beyond 0.9 m, none. Lost points lie at
+  y <= 0.75 m.
+- **Where it first fails.** Of the 1,466 lost points, 997 have no self-free
+  branch even at `sight_far`. The rest stop later (233 after `sight_near`, 105
+  after `pre_insert`, 87 after `sight_far`, 30 after `lift`, 14 after `insert`).
+- **Farther out nothing changes.** The full-sequence region still spans
+  x -0.8..0.8, y 0..1.0, z -0.70..0.95. At y = 0.8 and y = 1.0 the slices have
+  the same point count as before (542 and 141).
+- **Level 6 is still empty** for the same reason as before: the `strict` preset
+  has no carry tilt.
+
+**Limits specific to this run**
+- Sphere self-collision only: the arm is not checked against the cell, and the
+  conservative spheres may remove marginal points.
+- Jaws are modelled open throughout. After `insert` they close on the tray, and
+  the tray is not modelled.
+- Chain continuity between phases is still not enforced; a point can pass each
+  phase on a different IK branch.
+- Remote scratch: the script, a 0.2 m trial and the result are in
+  `/workspace/robot-program/_reach/` on the program host.
+
+**Reproduce**
+
+```powershell
+$R = '.agent-workspace/renders/reach_volume'
+cd program
+.\.crosshost\sync.ps1 ..\.agent-workspace\tools\reach_volume\reach_volume_curobo.py /workspace/robot-program/_reach
+# remote: python3 _reach/reach_volume_curobo.py --out _reach/reach_volume_curobo.npz   (~40 s)
+.\.crosshost\fetch.ps1 /workspace/robot-program/_reach/reach_volume_curobo.npz ..\.agent-workspace\renders\reach_volume\
+cd ..
+python .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_volume.py --npz $R/reach_volume_curobo.npz --html $R/reach_volume_curobo.html
+python .agent-workspace/tools/reach_volume/plot_reach_slices.py --npz $R/reach_volume_curobo.npz --html $R/reach_slices_curobo.html
+```
