+# M3 — Collision + path feasibility — **done** (2026-10-03 – 2026-10-10)
+
+**Triggered 2026-10-03** by the user ("Starts M3"): M6 is next and needs
+planned paths, which is this milestone's written trigger.
+
+findings/04 §5 is explicit that reachability proves neither. cuRobo is the
+authority and **will** reduce the 259/259.
+
+This is the most expensive item and the most likely to churn, since it consumes
+geometry that is still moving. It is also the gate for M2's 3c.
+
+**Trigger:** a planned path is needed (M6), M2's 3c fires, or a slot the IK
+accepts turns out to be blocked by something in the way. The strict preset
+(D23) makes this likelier: if collision removes `outgoing/L3/C0` or `C5`,
+switch to `recommended`.
+
+## Known inputs (probed 2026-10-03, program host)
+
+- cuRobo v2 `0.7.9.post1.dev75` on `llm-wiki`, RTX 5070, torch 2.7 cu128;
+  EAIK, trimesh and numpy 1.26 are present too.
+- `RobotCollisionChecker(Cfg.load_from_config(robot_config, scene_model))` takes
+  joint batches and returns `(scene_dist, self_dist)`. Scene poses are
+  **wxyz**; plan.md and `export_shapes.py` use xyzw.
+- `/ReKep-ros/rekep/rekep/curobo_node.py` is the user's v2 port. It loads
+  `tm5s_v5.yml` and fills the empty `gripper` slot with the forward-kinematics
+  spheres of `egu50_v2.yml`, using `kinematics_config.update_link_spheres`,
+  plus `update_link_mesh` for exact meshes. `attached_object` holds the tray.
+  Scenes are built as `Scene(cuboid=[Cuboid(...)])` from xyzw dicts.
+- Sphere radii on the plate are ~34 mm, but the plate is 10 mm thick and the
+  corridor is 32.5 mm. **Spheres alone will flag every insert.** Plate-in-jig
+  phases need the mesh distance.
+- `export_shapes.py` skips referenced prims (jigs, trays, robot), so a stage
+  export lacks the very obstacles that matter.
+
+## Design (approved 2026-10-03: cell_core world, mesh verdict, m = 5 mm)
+
+### How the cell_core world is built, and how it differs from a USD export
+
+The new module is `cell_core/scene.py`. It follows the same chain the builder
+uses, but stops at boxes instead of USD prims:
+
+`CellConfig` → `env_adapter.generator_kwargs` / `geometry` (rack origins, shelf
+heights, slot frames) → named cuboids (centre, size, xyzw, in the robot-base
+frame).
+
+Each part comes from:
+
+- **Shelves and legs:** from the rack dims in the config.
+- **Jigs and trays:** box dims from `assets.py` (measured from the USD assets),
+  placed at the `enumerate_slots` frames.
+- **Table, table jig and robot base:** from the same config.
+
+Legs (cylinders) are written as boxes that enclose them, which over-states them
+by at most 8 mm. That is safe, and the scene stays one primitive type.
+
+| | cell_core scene | USD export (`export_shapes.py`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Source | the config the sweep and IK are judged on | the stage the builder wrote |
+| Jigs, trays | included (boxes from `assets.py`) | **missing** (referenced prims are skipped) |
+| Per-phase edits (remove target tray, attach it) | by name, in Python | hand-edit the YAML |
+| Needs the sim host | no | yes, a rebuild and export per config change |
+| Fidelity | boxes: jig columns and tray as boxes, legs enclosed | exact native shapes, but only the natives |
+| Drift guard | test against `measured/*.json` | is itself the measurement |
+
+**Drift guard.** The measured fixtures already hold world bounding boxes for
+every native prim (shelves, legs, table top, robot base) and world poses for
+every jig and tray. A local test compares the cell_core scene with them:
+boxes at bbox level, jigs and trays at pose level. It runs on all three
+presets, with the lateral tolerance from D22. This is the check that caught the
+308 mm rack error.
+
+### Design points
+1. **World from `cell_core`.** Add `cell_core/scene.py`, pure Python. It turns a
+   `CellConfig` into named cuboids (xyzw, plan.md form): rack shelves, uprights,
+   jigs (base and columns), trays, table, table jig, robot base and legs, and
+   ground. A one-line adapter converts to cuRobo wxyz. It is tested locally
+   against `isaacsim/tests/measured/*.json`.
+2. **Per-phase world.** The target tray stays in the world up to `insert`. From
+   `lift` it moves to `attached_object` (tray box from `assets.py`). Release
+   mirrors this.
+3. **Robot model.** `tm5s_v5.yml` plus the `egu50_v2` gripper, as in
+   `curobo_node.py`. The **mesh** distance is the verdict; sphere distances are
+   reported only.
+4. **Joints from EAIK.** `reach_sweep` already enumerates every analytic branch
+   per slot and phase. Each branch is collision-checked, so no cuRobo IK is
+   involved. A slot passes if one branch is collision-free at all of
+   `pre_insert`, `insert` and `lift` (this also gives the no-elbow-flip check).
+5. **Margins.** Contact with the target slot's jig or tray fails at 0 mm (D17
+   already budgets that corridor). Everything else needs at least the margin
+   **m = 5 mm**. Self-collision fails at 0 mm.
+6. **Where it runs.** A new `program/collision/check_cell.py` runs on the
+   program host and writes a JSON report (per slot, phase and branch: distances
+   and the nearest obstacle name). `evaluate.py` gains a `collision` check that
+   reads that report, and skips it locally.
+7. **Exit.** Every strict slot has a passing branch. If `outgoing/L3/C0` or `C5`
+   fails, switch to `recommended` (D23).
+
+## Tasks
+
+- [x] Generate a cuRobo world config from `cell_core`, with the same primitives
+      as the obstacle YAML in plan.md (one geometry source)
+      — `cell_core/scene.py` (`cell_boxes`, `phase_scene`, `to_curobo_scene`),
+      `shared/tests/test_scene.py` (27, mutation 27/27), drift test
+      `isaacsim/tests/test_measured_scene.py` (21 over 3 presets, mutation 10/10).
+      Suite 418 passed, 2 skipped.
+- [x] Collision-check every pose the harness reaches: shelves, uprights,
+      neighbour jigs, trays in adjacent slots, self-collision
+      — checker written: `program/collision/check_cell.py` (pure parts tested in
+      `program/tests/test_check_cell.py`, 24, mutation 19/19,
+      `scratch/mutate_m3_checker.py`). Host run: `cmd_20261003_collision_strict.sh`.
