+# Todo — one file per milestone
+
+The detailed task lists. The coarse, slow-moving view is
+[../roadmap.md](../roadmap.md); the settled choices are in
+[../decisions/001-architecture-and-scope.md](../decisions/001-architecture-and-scope.md).
+
+**Updated:** 2026-10-10
+
+| # | File | State |
+|---|------|-------|
+| M0 | [M0-cell-model.md](M0-cell-model.md) | done |
+| M1 | [M1-sim-env-eval.md](M1-sim-env-eval.md) | done |
+| M2 | [M2-tilt-table-friction.md](M2-tilt-table-friction.md) | core done; rest contingent |
+| M3 | [M3-collision-path.md](M3-collision-path.md) | **done** |
+| M4 | [M4-locating.md](M4-locating.md) | done (D25–D27) |
+| M5 | [M5-scanning.md](M5-scanning.md) | not started |
+| M6 | [M6-motion-exec.md](M6-motion-exec.md) | not started |
+| M7 | [M7-orchestration.md](M7-orchestration.md) | not started |
+| M8 | [M8-real-cell.md](M8-real-cell.md) | not started |
+
+## How these files are kept
+
+- Each milestone file holds its own tasks, results and notes. Work on M*n*
+  updates only `Mn-*.md`, plus the status table above.
+- A closed milestone's file stays as the record. It is not rewritten.
+- Cross-milestone items live in the milestone that has to *do* them. The other
+  one links to it.
+- Nothing is deleted when it is superseded. Strike it through and say why.
+
+## Triage rule (user, binding)
+
+*"You will not do the tasks with low mandatory but with high effort or uncertain
+degree, they will be done only if the problem happened."*
+
+Each item is rated on three axes:
+
+- **Mandatory:** does the system fail without it?
+- **Effort:** how much work is it?
+- **Uncertain:** how likely is the answer to be wrong, or to churn?
+
+**Low mandatory with high effort or high uncertainty means contingent.**
+Contingent work is not cancelled and not forgotten. It is written down with the
+symptom that would trigger it, and it stays unbuilt until that symptom appears.
+
+The reason is that a speculative fix is usually the wrong fix. A tilt that fouls
+the shelf has at least four remedies, and choosing between them before seeing
+the actual violation means choosing blind. Passing such a check on *this* cell
+also proves nothing about the next one, and the cell is expected to keep
+changing.
+
+| Item | Milestone | Mand. | Effort | Uncert. | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `carry_tilt` field; carry and release poses | M2 | high | low | low | done |
+| Prove a tilt *range* stays reachable | M2 | high | low | low | done |
+| Tilted pose does not foul the shelf above | M2 | low | med | **high** | contingent |
+| Table position and height sweep | M2 | **low** | med | high | contingent (already satisfied) |
+| Friction: value, range, measurement rig | M2 | low | high | **high** | contingent |
+| cuRobo collision world | M3 | med | **high** | med | ~~contingent~~ triggered 2026-10-03 (M6 needs paths; user) |
+| Build the Isaac Sim stage from a preset | M1 | high | med | med | done |
+| Measure the stage back against the config | M1 | high | low | low | done |
+| Closer (0.12 m) read with a camera raise | M4 | low | med | high | contingent |
+| Lens distortion in the sim renders | M4 | low | med | high | contingent |
+
+## Standing notes
+
+- **Run CrossHost from the matching repo directory** (`isaacsim/` or
+  `program/`). The terminal's working directory persists, so `cd` to an
+  absolute path first. If a command gives no output and then times out, the host
+  may be down: ask the user (D13).
+- **Things that trip the CrossHost approval dialog:** `at` followed by a space
+  (it turns up in ordinary prose), `python3 -c`, `PYTHONPATH`, and `rm` with
+  `-r`/`-f`. Prefer a synced `.py` file over `-c`, and let the script fix its own
+  `sys.path`. Triggering the dialog is acceptable when the command is genuinely
+  needed.
+- **`sync.ps1 <dir> <remote>` puts the directory at `<remote>/<dir-leaf>`.**
+  That is documented behaviour, not a bug.
+- **EAIK is installed locally.** The whole reachability evaluation is a local
+  one-command operation (see M1).
+- **The agent runs no git commands (D12).** Deleting files needs the user's OK.
