++## D25 — M4 acceptance: the far read is not judged on pitch; RMSE cut 2 px — *JUDGED part SUPERSEDED by D27*
++
++User decision, 2026-09-30, after the first full locate run on `strict`
++(74 renders, `cmd_20260930_locate_strict.sh`). It supersedes two parts of the
++approved M4 design: that every read is judged on all four axes, and my own
++`MAX_RMSE_PX = 1.0`.
++
++What the first run showed (`renders/strict/results.json`):
++- 74/74 boards found, correct id, coverage 1.00. Vertical ≤ 0.031 mm, lateral
++  ≤ 0.043 mm, yaw ≤ 0.27°.
++- **Far-read pitch** (0.35 m) scatters with sd 0.32° on incoming and 0.59° on
++  outgoing. 4 outgoing far reads exceed ½·budget (−1.37° to −1.65° against
++  1.274°). Near-read pitch has sd 0.13° and a worst of −0.35°. Pitch is tilt
++  about the strip's long axis. A 20 mm tall 4×1 strip gives little leverage on
++  it: at 0.35 m, 1° is about 0.7 px of top/bottom width difference.
