++## D26 — Locating renders: AA off, linear tone map, linear-light grey
++
++User request, 2026-10-03: fix the D25 depth bias. Suggested options: DLSS off
++or DLAA, auto exposure off or a linear tone map, linearize the sRGB.
++Evidence is in `findings/05` §4–§5.
++
++Decision: `render_locating.py` renders every locating image with:
++- **AA off.** `SimulationApp({"anti_aliasing": 0})`, plus
++  `/rtx-transient/post/aa/limitedOps = false` and `/rtx/post/aa/op = 0`.
++  Isaac puts DLSS back if either of the first two is missing.
++- **Linear tone map.** `/rtx/post/tonemap/op = 1` instead of ACES (6).
++  It is re-applied before every frame, because Isaac reverts it once at startup.
++- **Linear-light grey.** Each RGB channel is sRGB-decoded first, then mixed
++  with luma 0.299/0.587/0.114 into an 8-bit PNG (`detector_grey`).
++- Before each capture, the run checks that every setting is still in effect.
++  If any drifted, the run stops (`settings_drift`, SystemExit). The settings
++  are written to `truth.json` (`render_settings`).
++
++Rejected or not needed:
++- **DLAA** (aa/op 4) leaves almost all of the bias: mean z/Z +0.168 %, against
++  +0.205 % for DLSS.
