++**Conclusion:** the **top layer of both racks is at or beyond the reach limit at
++insertion depth**, and the outgoing rack's top outer corners are unreachable
++outright. Sighting those same slots is easy (0.75–0.79 m) — the robot can *see*
++slots it cannot *service*.
++
++This is a distance-sphere argument only; it ignores the orientation constraint
++(the flange must point horizontally into the shelf, which consumes wrist DOF
++near full extension) and joint limits, both of which make it **worse**, not
++better. It must be settled by an actual IK sweep, not by this arithmetic — see
++the proposed reachability map.
