++# 05 — AprilGrid detection error in the AprilGrid frame (strict, 2026-10-02)
++
++## 1. Setup
++
++- Renders: strict stage, 37 slots × {far 0.35 m, near 0.2743 m} = 74 reads
++  (`render_locating.py`, M4 task 6). Truth `truth.json` sha `c19883ef…5fe0`.
++- Detector: `aprilgrid_detector` on the program host, via
++  `program/locating/locate.py` (sha `7d0f65e9…f3f0`), focal config 6
++  (fx 2680.38, fy 2680.74), no distortion. Command
++  `program/.crosshost/commands/cmd_20261002_board_errors.sh`; outputs
++  `renders/strict/board_errors.{json,out}`.
++- Frame: the **true** board frame (detector convention): origin top-left of
++  tag 0, x along PNG columns (long axis of the strip), y down the rows, z into
++  the label. `E = T_true⁻¹ · T_measured`:
++  - x, y, z = translation of E;
++  - rx, ry, rz = `Rotation.from_matrix(E_R).as_euler("xyz")` (extrinsic xyz), deg;
++  - tilt, azimuth, roll = the user's `euler_to_tilt_azimuth_roll(·, 'xyz')`,
++    copied verbatim into `locate.py`.
++- Cross-check: recomputed locally from `accept.json` vs `truth.json`; identical.
++
++## 2. Results
++
++mean ± sd, worst |value| (slot):
++
++| read | x mm | y mm | z mm | rx ° | ry ° | rz ° | tilt ° |
++|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
++| far  | +0.025 ± 0.010, +0.039 (out/L3/C4) | +0.004 ± 0.010, +0.025 (out/L1/C2) | +0.754 ± 0.163, +1.130 (out/L0/C5) | +0.535 ± 0.523, +1.650 (out/L3/C2) | +0.140 ± 0.082, +0.273 (in/L2/C1) | +0.004 ± 0.009, +0.018 | 0.663 ± 0.384, 1.652 |
++| near | +0.032 ± 0.006, +0.043 (out/L1/C4) | +0.019 ± 0.008, +0.031 (in/L1/C0) | +0.648 ± 0.089, +0.792 (out/L1/C1) | +0.069 ± 0.142, +0.348 (out/L1/C3) | +0.181 ± 0.046, +0.262 (out/L1/C1) | −0.004 ± 0.009, −0.020 | 0.238 ± 0.058, 0.412 |
++
++By workspace (z mean, worst; rx mean ± sd, worst):
++
++| workspace | read | z mm | rx ° |
++|---|---|---|---|
++| incoming (12) | far  | +0.65, +0.91 | +0.44 ± 0.32, +0.83 |
++| incoming (12) | near | +0.56, +0.65 | +0.06 ± 0.14, +0.27 |
++| outgoing (24) | far  | +0.82, +1.13 | +0.60 ± 0.59, +1.65 |
++| outgoing (24) | near | +0.70, +0.79 | +0.09 ± 0.14, +0.35 |
++| table (1)     | far  | +0.38 | +0.05 |
++| table (1)     | near | +0.44 | −0.25 |
