++## 3. Reading the numbers
++
++- x, y, rz: < 0.05 mm and < 0.02° everywhere.
++- z: positive on every read, +0.4…+1.1 mm — a bias, analysed in §4.
++- rx (about the strip's long axis) is the weak rotation: far sd 0.52°, worst
++  1.65°; near cuts it ~4×. Same as the far-read pitch scatter of D25.
++- ry: a steady +0.14…+0.18° with little scatter.
++- Tilt/azimuth/roll: tilt < 2°, so azimuth is ill-defined (−166°…+89°) and
++  roll cancels it (azimuth + roll = rz within 0.02°). Reported per read, not
++  summarised.
++- Same numbers as the slot-axis errors with x = −lateral, y = −vertical,
++  z = depth, rx = −pitch, ry ≈ −yaw. M4 acceptance unchanged (PASS 74/74).
++
++## 4. Depth bias
++
++**Cause: the renderer, not the detector, the camera model or the scene.**
++Isaac's default DLSS upscaler (`/rtx/post/aa/op = 3`, auto mode) is the main
++cause. The ACES tone mapper (`/rtx/post/tonemap/op = 6`) adds a smaller part.
++Both make the black tag squares render slightly smaller. Smaller squares look
++farther away, so the depth estimate (z) comes out too large.
++
++### 4.1 What the bias looks like (74 strict reads, camera frame)
++
++- It is a scale on camera Z only: z_err / Z = +0.207 % far (sd 0.027) and
++  +0.183 % near. Lateral error is ≈ 0.03 mm, so it is not a whole-pose scale
++  (the fitted lateral scale is −0.09 %).
++- It differs by workspace (far/near): incoming +0.173/+0.155 %, outgoing
++  +0.226/+0.198 %, table +0.157/+0.146 %. So it is not a fixed offset.
++
++### 4.2 Where it comes from (pixels)
++
++- The distance between tags in the image matches the projected truth
++  (−0.006 %, +0.001 %). This rules out focal length, intrinsics, texture
++  scale, label size, truth poses and frames.
++- Each black square is ≈ 1 % smaller than the truth, shrunk about its own
++  centre. From edge profiles against the projected truth edges, each edge sits
++  0.78 px (far) and 0.92 px (near) inside the truth, 0.6–0.9 texel.
++  Brighter scenes shrink more: outgoing (white plateau 250, lifted black
++  level) shrinks more than incoming or table (243). corr(inset, detector z)
++  is 0.56 far and 0.81 near.
++- Size check: with the 16 corners at ±10 mm about tag centres at ±13.75 and
++  ±41.25 mm, a uniform per-tag shrink s shrinks the PnP scale by ≈ 0.175·s.
++  This predicts Z +0.18 % far and +0.16 % near; observed +0.21 % and +0.18 %.
++
++### 4.3 Test: turn each renderer stage off
++
++The same 4 reads (incoming/outgoing L1/C2, far/near) were re-rendered with
++[render_variant.py](../tools/render_variant.py) and run through the deployed
++`locate.py` on the program host.
++
++| variant | settings | edge inset (px, in/out) | z err in/far | in/near | out/far | out/near | mean z/Z |
++|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
++| base | DLSS + ACES (default) | 0.52–0.57 / 0.79–0.93 | +0.578 | +0.370 | +0.980 | +0.649 | **+0.205 %** |
++| linear | DLSS, tonemap op 1 | 0.28–0.31 / 0.63–0.74 | +0.274 | +0.280 | +0.659 | +0.540 | +0.142 % |
++| noaa | AA off, ACES | 0.24–0.28 / 0.37–0.47 | −0.065 | +0.143 | +0.007 | +0.240 | **+0.031 %** |
++| noaa + linear | AA off, tonemap op 1 | 0.08–0.10 / 0.31–0.40 | −0.054 | +0.075 | −0.050 | +0.192 | +0.017 % |
++
++(z errors in mm; edge inset measured in sRGB values at the 50 % level.)
++
++- With DLSS off, the bias drops from +0.205 % to +0.031 %: from 0.4–1.0 mm to
++  −0.07…+0.24 mm. DLSS accounts for ≈ 85 % of the bias.
++- Turning ACES off as well removes a little more. What remains on outgoing
++  comes from whites clipping at 255 there, which shifts the edge toward the
++  black side.
++- n = 4 reads per variant; the direction and size are consistent on all four.
++
++### 4.4 Implications
++
++- This is a rendering artifact. A real camera has no DLSS, so its depth bias
++  will be different (lens blur, sensor and exposure instead). Do not carry the
++  +0.2 % into the real-camera error budget, and do not correct for it in
++  `locate.py`.
++- To make sim depth meaningful, `render_locating` should render with
++  anti-aliasing off (and optionally a linear tone map). This is a render-config
++  change and needs a decision record. Otherwise depth stays "reported, not
++  judged" (D25).
++- **Gotcha:** setting `/rtx/post/aa/op = 0` alone is silently undone.
++  - `SimulationApp`'s default `anti_aliasing: 3` re-applies DLSS.
++  - `/rtx-transient/post/aa/limitedOps = True` (the default) also keeps
++    DLSS on.
++  - DLSS only stays off with `SimulationApp({"anti_aliasing": 0, …})` plus
++    `/rtx-transient/post/aa/limitedOps = false`. This is the same pair that
++    `omni.syntheticdata`'s test configs use. The first two variant runs
++    (`var_noaa`, `var_noaa_linear`) were silently still DLSS and are
++    discarded.
++- Side note: the current sim-host strict stage (`cell.usd` sha 0c915567…,
++  rebuilt with the ground plane) renders darker than the original strict
++  renders (incoming grey 142 vs ≈ 176–196). Variants were therefore compared
++  with `var_base`, not with the original 74 renders.
++- The render logs' 16 "cannot create a joint between static bodies" PhysX
++  errors also appear in the original strict render log. They come from
++  freezing the rigid bodies and are not new.
++
