++# M1 — Config drives the sim; evaluation re-runs on one command — **done**
++
++**Closed:** 2026-09-29. This file is the record and is not rewritten.
++
++The cell setup is expected to keep changing: robot height, jig gap, rack
++geometry, table. So the deliverable is not one built environment but the ability
++to re-evaluate any environment for free.
++
++## The user's governing constraint (Q2)
++
++*"The environment setup might change anytime"* is the governing constraint, not
++a footnote. It demotes building any one environment and promotes being able to
++re-evaluate any environment.
++
++The parameters that must be free to move without code edits: robot height, jig
++gap, rack distances, layer heights, jig counts, rack widths, table position and
++height, standoffs, tilt and friction. All are `CellConfig` fields except
++friction (contingent, M2).
++
++**Order of work:**
++1. One geometry source.
++2. Evaluation on one command.
++3. Tilt, core only (M2).
++4. Sim stage from a preset.
++
++Everything else happens on demand, per the triage in [README.md](README.md).
++
