++
++## 1. Retire `cell_geometry.py`: one geometry source, not two — **done**
++
++- [x] Replace `import cell_geometry as G` with the vendored `cell_core`
++- [x] Add `--preset` / `--config`; keep `--origin-z` and `--near-standoff` as
++      overrides, since the sensitivity scans need to sweep them freely
++- [x] Sync the vendored `cell_core` to the program host with the sweep
++- [x] **Re-ran and verified identical:** 35/37, with the same two blocked slots
++      at `outgoing/L3/{C0,C5}` in the same phases. Then diffed row by row:
++      **222/222 identical** in `status`, `horiz`, `z` and `shoulder_r`
++- [x] Deleted `cell_geometry.py` and `test_port_equivalence.py`; corrected
++      findings/04 §6
++
++The row-level diff was the point. A matching 35/37 would not have settled it:
++two runs can agree on a count while disagreeing about which slots.
++`compare_sweeps.py` is kept for exactly this.
++
++## 2. `evaluate.py`: the whole evaluation, one command, any config — **done**
++
++- [x] `python evaluate.py --preset recommended` runs the geometry audit,
++      clearances, tolerance budget and reachability over every slot and phase,
++      and gives one PASS/FAIL
++- [x] Machine-readable report beside the human one
++- [x] `--baseline <report>` diffs against a previous run and names what moved
++- [x] `--scan origin_z=0.60:0.85:0.025` for parameter sweeps
++- [x] ~~Runs on the program host (needs EAIK)~~. **EAIK is installed locally.**
++      The whole evaluation runs here in about a minute.
++- [x] Baseline reports in `.agent-workspace/baselines/`
++
++What was built:
++
++- `shared/cell_core/audit.py`: 15 geometry checks, pure arithmetic, vendored.
++  It **never raises**. A broken config comes back as a report naming the failed
++  check, because a traceback cannot be diffed against a baseline.
++- `config.SCAN_PARAMS` + `apply_override`: a registry of the quantities a sweep
++  may vary. A typo is a clear error instead of a silently misapplied value.
++- `geometry.fov_half_width`: the binding dimension for whether the grid fits in
++  frame, since the grid is wider than it is tall.
++- `.agent-workspace/tools/evaluate.py`: audit, IK sweep, report, diff and scan.
++
++Worth remembering:
++
++- **A skipped check is not a passing check.** `--no-reach` still prints
++  `VERDICT: PASS`, but under it prints `NOT CHECKED: reachability`.
++- **`reach_sphere_margin` is a trend figure, not clearance.** Pass/fail always
++  comes from the IK. It can read negative while every slot is reachable.
++- **`evaluate.py` writes `--json` before diffing `--baseline`.** Giving both the
++  same path makes it diff the new report against itself.
